{"title": "Tommy Dorfman", "pageid": 55749443, "revid": 1379364192, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tommy_Dorfman", "lang": "en", "year": 1992, "short_description": "American actress (born 1992)", "wikidata_id": "Q30105342", "is_disambiguation": false, "infobox": {"Born": ["(1992-05-13) May 13, 1992", "Atlanta, Georgia, U.S."], "Education": "Fordham University", "Occupation": "Actress", "Years active": "2009–present", "Relatives": "Andi Dorfman (cousin)"}, "facts": {"directors": [], "writers": [], "producers": [], "cast": [], "music": [], "cinematography": [], "editors": [], "production_companies": [], "distributors": [], "release_dates": [], "runtime_minutes": null, "countries": [], "languages": [], "budget": [], "box_office": [], "based_on": []}, "text": {"lead": "Tommy Dorfman (born May 13, 1992) is an American actress, best known for playing Ryan Shaver in the Netflix series 13 Reasons Why (2017).", "plot": "", "cast": "", "production": "", "release": "", "reception": "", "themes": ""}, "sections": {"Lead": "Tommy Dorfman (born May 13, 1992) is an American actress, best known for playing Ryan Shaver in the Netflix series 13 Reasons Why (2017).", "Early life and education": "Dorfman was born and raised in Atlanta, Georgia, to a Jewish family. Her cousin is Andi Dorfman, a former contestant on The Bachelorette. Dorfman graduated from Fordham University 's drama program in 2015 with a B.A. in theatre arts.", "Career": "After graduating from university, Dorfman was cast in the role of Ryan Shaver on the Netflix drama 13 Reasons Why, which premiered in 2017. Also that year, she helped design a fashion collection with ASOS, and in October was honored with the Rising Star Award by GLAAD.\nIn the spring of 2019, Dorfman made her New York theatrical debut in The New Group 's production of Jeremy O. Harris 's play Daddy, directed by Danya Taymor.\nIn 2024 she directed and co-wrote the film I Wish You All the Best, about a teen's coming out as non-binary, which received positive reviews. Dorfman's direction was praised by Variety as making \"an attractive look and smooth pace.\"\nIn 2025, she starred in the Off-Broadway production of Becoming Eve by Emil Weinstein based on the memoir by Abby Chava Stein, playing the role of Chava. For her performance, Dorfman was nominated for the 2025 Drama League Award for Distinguished Performance and the 2026 Dorian Award for Outstanding Lead Performance in an Off-Broadway Production.", "Personal life": "Dorfman is queer. Dorfman and Peter Zurkuhlen became engaged in April 2015 and married in Portland, Maine, on November 12, 2016. In July 2021, Dorfman revealed she and Zurkuhlen had divorced but remain friends.\nIn November 2017, Dorfman came out as non-binary and began using they pronouns. On July 22, 2021, Dorfman came out as a transgender woman and began using she pronouns. She revealed in an interview that she had already been \"privately identifying and living as a woman\" for almost a year. She chose to retain her birth name of Tommy, to which she feels \"very connected\" and which honors her mother's brother who died when Dorfman was a month old. In April 2022, Dorfman identified as a lesbian.\nIn May 2024, Dorfman revealed that she had secretly eloped with her girlfriend, Elise Williams, in Malibu, California, around late 2023."}, "cast_list": [], "plot_word_count": 0, "categories": ["Living people", "1992 births", "Jewish American actresses", "Actresses from Atlanta", "American television actresses", "Fordham University alumni", "American transgender actresses", "LGBTQ people from Georgia (U.S. state)", "Transgender Jews", "21st-century American Jews", "21st-century American LGBTQ people", "21st-century American actresses", "Alumni of the Paideia School", "Transgender lesbians", "Jewish LGBTQ women", "American lesbian actresses"], "external": {}, "external_links": ["https://twitter.com/tommydorfmans/status/995586490708066305", "https://www.advocate.com/arts-entertainment/2017/10/17/out-13-reasons-why-star-tommy-dorfman-responds-brazilian-homophobia", "https://web.archive.org/web/20200827090322/https://www.advocate.com/arts-entertainment/2017/10/17/out-13-reasons-why-star-tommy-dorfman-responds-brazilian-homophobia", "https://i-d.co/article/tommy-dorfman-is-the-unapologetically-queer-actor-from-13-reasons-why/", "https://web.archive.org/web/20200827090323/https://i-d.vice.com/en_us/article/7xbbza/tommy-dorfman-is-the-unapologetically-queer-actor-from-13-reasons-why", "https://web.archive.org/web/20220920173217/https://www.out.com/celebs/2022/4/13/tommy-dorfman-recipe-for-change-jubilee-youtube-clip-jewish-trans-identities-lgbt-community", "https://news.fordham.edu/fordham-magazine/fordham-theatre-grad-honored-glaad/", "https://web.archive.org/web/20200827090328/https://news.fordham.edu/fordham-magazine/fordham-theatre-grad-honored-glaad/", "http://www.papermag.com/beautiful-people-tommy-dorfman-1-2488383804.html", "https://web.archive.org/web/20190619092619/http://www.papermag.com/beautiful-people-tommy-dorfman-1-2488383804.html", "https://www.mtv.co.uk/news/rmfyt5/13-reasons-whys-tommy-dorfman-has-released-an-awesome-fashion-collection", "https://web.archive.org/web/20200827090332/http://www.mtv.co.uk/13-reasons-why/news/13-reasons-whys-tommy-dorfman-has-released-an-awesome-fashion-collection", "https://vineyardtheatre.org/archive/daddy/", "https://variety.com/2025/film/reviews/i-wish-you-all-the-best-review-1236571044/", "https://www.nytw.org/show/becoming-eve/", "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/04/11/theater/review-becoming-eve.html", "https://playbill.com/article/photos-2025-drama-league-awards-with-winners-nicole-scherzinger-sam-pinkleton-more", "https://newyorktheater.me/2026/06/01/2026-dorian-theater-award-winners-schmigadoon-prince-faggot-ragtime-joshua-junior-quincy-qween/", "https://www.popsugar.com/node/43522971", "https://web.archive.org/web/20220103131335/https://time.com/6081874/tommy-dorfman-interview/", "https://time.com/6081874/t